---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { BUSINESS, MAILTO_HREF } from "@/consts";

const trail = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy/" },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How Skip Bits handles your information.">
  <div class="wrap max-w-3xl py-10">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        This website is run by {BUSINESS.name}, a trading name of {BUSINESS.legalName} (company no.
        {BUSINESS.companyNumber}), {BUSINESS.addressLines.slice(1).join(", ")}.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display pt-4 text-2xl">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The website has no forms or accounts and doesn't ask for any personal information. Our web host may keep
        standard server logs (such as IP addresses) for security.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display pt-4 text-2xl">Website analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use two analytics services to see how the site is used and where it can be improved.
        <strong>Google Analytics</strong> records which pages are visited, how visitors arrived and roughly where they
        are, and, only if you choose Accept in the cookie banner, sets first-party cookies (<code>_ga</code> and
        <code>_ga_*</code>) to tell repeat visits apart.
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> records how pages are used — clicks, scrolling and mouse movement — and can
        replay a page visit as an anonymous recording. Clarity runs without cookies for visitors in the UK and Europe,
        and anything typed into the search box or other fields is masked before it leaves your browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        Neither service is used for advertising, and we don't try to identify individual visitors. Google Analytics cookies are used only with your consent: until you accept them, or if you choose No
        thanks, Google Analytics sets no cookies and sends only anonymous, cookieless measurements. You can
        change your choice at any time with Cookie settings at the foot of any page. For Clarity and those
        cookieless measurements we rely on our legitimate interest in improving the website. Google Analytics keeps visit data for no more than 14 months.
        Clarity keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated reports for up to 13 months. You can block or delete
        cookies in your browser settings, or opt out of Google Analytics with Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-brand-600 underline">browser add-on</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you phone or email us, we'll use the details you give us — your name, contact details and what you're
        enquiring about — to answer your enquiry and, if you order, to supply and invoice the parts. We keep these
        records for as long as we need them for that and for our accounts.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display pt-4 text-2xl">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you by emailing
        <a href={MAILTO_HREF} class="text-brand-600 underline">{BUSINESS.email}</a>. If you're unhappy with how we've
        handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
